<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yaroslav Sviatoslavich</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1129</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yaroslav Sviatoslavich was a Rurikid prince, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sviatoslav-ii-of-kiev">Sviatoslav II of Kiev</a>, who ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murom">Murom</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ryazan">Ryazan</a> and briefly <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chernigov">Chernigov</a>. His descendants formed the ruling lines of the north-eastern lands of Murom and Ryazan, which separated into two principalities around 1129.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yaroslav-sviatoslavich.jpg" alt="Yaroslav Sviatoslavich" width="320" height="428" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SeikoEn · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Principalities_of_Kievan_Rus%27_(1054-1132).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
